        "title": "Soil Microbiology: Bacteria, Fungi, Mycorrhizae, Soil Food Web",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SOM + Plant Residue + Root Exudates\n  (primary energy source)\n          |\n          v\n  BACTERIA + FUNGI (decomposers; primary consumers)\n     |          |\n     |          +--- FUNGAL FEEDERS (nematodes, mites, collembolans)\n     |\n     v\n  PROTOZOA (flagellates, amoebae, ciliates)\n     |       Graze bacteria; mineralize N in the process\n     |\n     v\n  NEMATODE PREDATORS (feeding on protozoa + other nematodes)\n     |\n     v\n  MITES + COLLEMBOLA (microarthropods)\n  ENCHYTRAEIDS (potworms)\n     |\n     v\n  EARTHWORMS + MILLIPEDES + BEETLES\n  (macrofauna; physical soil engineers)\n     |\n     v\n  SMALL INVERTEBRATE PREDATORS (centipedes, predatory beetles)\n          |\n          v\n  BIRDS, MAMMALS, MOLES (consume soil invertebrates)\n```"
    }
